screens.text_md:
When threads run at the same time, their steps interleave in ways you don't control. Three problems follow:

- **race conditions**: threads touch the same data in an inconsistent order;
- **deadlocks**: two threads each wait for something the other holds;
- **bugs that appear only sometimes**, depending on timing.

Rust's ownership and type system prevent data races at compile time; the rest of this chapter shows the tools that make sharing safe. Design results so their order doesn't depend on timing, as in Screen 3.

